From 5e08ee075e021acee18645780f2ae145c461ebf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:39:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fingerprint: aidl: a rejected finger keeps identifying

onAuthenticationFailed was passed on as onError(UNABLE_TO_PROCESS), as
HIDL did. fingerprint.c ends the operation on any error: the state went
to idle, an under-display touch target went away and nothing started
identifying again, while the HAL still waited for a finger. On the lock
screen, one wrong finger left no way to use the sensor until the screen
was turned off and on again; fprintd clients got verify-unknown-error
instead of verify-no-match.

The AIDL operation goes on after a rejected touch, so report it as
finger id 0, which fingerprint.c takes as "not recognized" while it keeps
identifying.
---
 src/fingerprint_binder_aidl.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fingerprint_binder_aidl.c b/src/fingerprint_binder_aidl.c
index dd29998..df7b942 100644
--- a/src/fingerprint_binder_aidl.c
+++ b/src/fingerprint_binder_aidl.c
@@ -657,9 +657,16 @@ fingerprint_aidl_handle_authentication_failed(BiomFingerprintAidl* self)
 {
     g_debug("onAuthenticationFailed");
 
-    /* reported like HIDL does, as a non fatal UNABLE_TO_PROCESS */
-    if (self->callbacks.error)
-        self->callbacks.error(self->user_data, FINGERPRINT_ERROR_UNABLE_TO_PROCESS, 0);
+    /*
+     * A rejected touch. The AIDL operation goes on (it only ends with
+     * onAuthenticationSucceeded, onError or a lockout), so this must not end
+     * it in fingerprint.c either: an error there sets the state to idle, the
+     * touch target goes away and nothing starts identifying again, while the
+     * HAL is still waiting for a finger. fingerprint.c reports finger id 0 as
+     * "not recognized" and keeps identifying.
+     */
+    if (self->callbacks.authenticated)
+        self->callbacks.authenticated(self->user_data, 0, 0);
 
     return GBINDER_STATUS_OK;
 }
